        "body": "This unit focuses on toys, classroom materials, object handling, container play, simple adult-led exchange routines, and clean-up participation.\n\nFor PG children, toys are real objects for action, exploration, and classroom routine participation. Children experience toy language by looking, touching, holding, giving, taking, putting toys in, taking toys out, opening and closing containers, and joining short adult-supported routines.\n\nAt this age, the unit should remain concrete, physical, predictable, and routine-based. Children are not expected to name toys independently, answer location questions, use request chunks verbally, or produce spatial sentences. Any verbal imitation is treated as emerging language, not as a required outcome."
